.TH "CSVKIT" "1" "Sep 15, 2026" "2.2.0" "csvkit"
.SH NAME
csvkit \- csvkit Documentation
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Display the installed csvkit version and available command\-line tools:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
usage: csvkit [\-h] [\-V]

options:
  \-h, \-\-help     show this help message and exit
  \-V, \-\-version  show program\(aqs version number and exit
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
With no arguments, \fBcsvkit\fP displays the same overview as \fB\-\-help\fP\&.
The version and tool names come from the installed csvkit package. The overview
lists tools alphabetically and includes an example of getting help for a tool.
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
List the available tools:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
csvkit
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Print only the installed version:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
csvkit \-\-version
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Run tools directly, for example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
csvcut \-\-help
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The overview command does not accept CSV input or dispatch subcommands.
